id: pm-o74zyh
title: "The documented pm get --json to pm update --stdin-json round trip refuses system-maintained metadata: a claimed item's claim_principal and any format-bumped item's pm_format_version are rejected as core fields"
description: "Found while implementing pm-gh1713 (2026-11-14). docs/COMMANDS.md promises a lossless get, edit, update round trip through --stdin-json. The document adapter in src/sdk/structured-mutations.ts skips a short list of read-only keys (created_at, updated_at, author, collection_counts and similar) and turns every key outside CORE_ITEM_FIELD_KEYS into an extension --field assignment. System-maintained metadata is in neither list, so the round trip fails with core_item_field_requires_dedicated_flag for: claim_principal, present on every item a detected agent harness claimed (reproduced on 2026.11.13: pm claim, pm get --json, pm update --stdin-json); pm_format_version, present on every item with linked-test editor stamps (format 2) or setup entries (format 3); test_runs, the recorded linked-test run summaries. pm-gh1713 adds deferred_fields, which an imported item carries until it is curated, so the defect would hit every mirrored item. Expected: system-maintained keys are read-only in the document adapter, exactly like updated_at and author, and a create document's deferred_fields maps to the create deferral options so a strict tracker can recreate it. Duplicate check: searched stdin-json round trip claim_principal pm_format_version core item field requires dedicated flag; pm-stdin-schema-fields (closed) covered schema and extension fields only."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",round-trip,stdin-json
created_at: "2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:48.617Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:47.419Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:47.419Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "pm get --json piped into pm update --stdin-json succeeds for a claimed item, a format-2 or format-3 item and an item with deferred fields, without changing claim_principal, pm_format_version or test_runs; A create document carrying deferred_fields recreates the deferral (fields and reason) instead of refusing; A spec reproduces each refusal and proves the round trip"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "src/sdk/structured-mutations.ts treats pm_format_version, claim_principal, test_runs and deferred_fields as read-only document keys, so the host keeps deriving them. A create document's deferred_fields maps back to the defer and deferReason options: each field contributes only its own reason, explicit values, unsets and schema aliases override it through create's own unset parser, and an explicit reason in any spelling wins."
expected_result: "Piping pm get --json into pm update --stdin-json is lossless for claimed, format-bumped and deferred items"
actual_result: "Verified by spec: the adapter drops the system keys, and the built CLI round trip of a deferred strict item succeeds for update and for recreate"
